2 CONT  ANNA PEDERSDTR KÅDA b: 1608 in Kåda, Fister, Hjelmeland
2 CONT
2 CONT  BJØRN PEDERSEN HIDLE b: 1610 in Kåda, Fister, Hjelmeland
2 CONT
2 CONT  TORE PEDERSEN SKIFTUN SANDANGER b: 1616 in Kåda, Fister, Hjelmeland
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Peder Torson is named as the farmer of Kåda (2 1/3 laup smør)
2 CONT between 1603 and 1623.  According to the jordbok of 1617, he owned half the farm and leased the rest.  In 1624 and 1625, his widow is named as the operator of the farm.
2 CONT Peder was the lensmann in Hjelmeland skiprede for a time around 1614.
2 CONT He was summoned to court in 1616 because he had failed to appear at a forest survey (presumably a duty of the lensmann).  Peder claimed that he had not been informed of the survey.  The case was postponed and nothing further is he
2 CONC ard about it.
2 CONT Han åtte bl.a. det meste av øya Hidle, Sjernarøy, 5 laupar smør og 1/2 pd. korn.  Odelsjordeboka frå 1617 fortel at han åtte 1 laup smør og 1 vett korn i Hidle.  Dessutan hadde han 1 1/2 laupar smør til der som pantegods.
2 CONT Vidare åtte han 7 vetter korn i Lode, Kvia skipr. på Jæren (saman med sine medeigarar), 4 1/2 vetter korn i Fosse, Haugland skipr. på Jæren, 13 1/2 mrk. smør i Bjelland, Hjelmeland skipr., 1 1/2 laupar smør pantegods i Hovda, Hjel
2 CONC meland skipr. , 4 laupar smør pantegods i Indre Sandanger, Hjelmeland skipr., 1 1/2 laupar smør i Kåda, Hjelmeland skipr., 1/2 laup smør pantegods i Ytre Brekke, Sæbø skipr.
2 CONT Iflg. jordebok 1624 åtte Karen gods i 18 gardar, til saman rundt 20 laupar smør.
